Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.28,0:00:18.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roy Mustang observation journal...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.65,0:00:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.57,0:00:24.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As it turns out, I've been ordered by\NInternal Affairs to inspect my superior officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.95,0:00:29.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"In order that we may understand how your days are spent,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.58,0:00:34.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,those who are most suited to the task\Nare to conduct a top-secret inspection."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.34,0:00:37.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, Lieutenant Havoc,\Nyou're inspecting Colonel Mustang?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.42,0:00:40.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. But I can't investigate him\Nall on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.93,0:00:42.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want all of you to help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.64,0:00:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Saturday, 0946 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.39,0:00:51.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Mustang bluntly calls the documents before him that are due at noon to be a pain."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.69,0:00:54.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Similarly, Saturday, 1026 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.02,0:00:57.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel attempted to feed Lieutenant Hawkeye's dog."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.53,0:01:00.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Also, 1103 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.36,0:01:02.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel suddenly began to clean the windows."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.07,0:01:04.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Will he be able to\Nmeet his deadline?"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.49,0:01:07.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"1147 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.28,0:01:10.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel begins signing the documents as\Nhe makes a fuss about not having enough time."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.66,0:01:11.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"But he {\i1}did{\i0} have time."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.79,0:01:15.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"In the afternoon, the Colonel conducted an\Ninspection of the fire-fighting facilities around town."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.25,0:01:19.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"At this time, the Colonel received a letter\Nfrom the woman working at the flower shop."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.30,0:01:22.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"It appears that the letter is an invitation to a date."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.13,0:01:24.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Have witnessed tickets to a play."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.55,0:01:28.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"The Colonel readied to leave,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.55,0:01:29.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,saying he was gathering municipal intelligence, and would go directly home afterward."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.52,0:01:32.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Judging by his face,\Nhe is clearly going on a date."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.31,0:01:34.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.06,0:01:36.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The woman at the flower shop! You mean Grace?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.81,0:01:39.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought her attitude toward me had cooled off lately. Is that what's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.15,0:01:39.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"What's this, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.07,0:01:41.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were seeing that girl?"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.74,0:01:43.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"You're out of luck\Nagainst the Colonel."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.53,0:01:45.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I'm sorry to hear that. Please give up on her."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.53,0:01:46.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop making light of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.45,0:01:49.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"How could you guys\Nknow how I feel?!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.08,0:01:52.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"It's your fault you got dumped. No question about it."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.41,0:01:53.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Shut up, you big dope!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.71,0:01:55.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"No, you are!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.67,0:01:55.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"What did you call me?!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.71,0:01:56.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Attaboy, get him, get him!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.92,0:01:59.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Don't be so rough on each other.\NLet's all get along."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.46,0:02:00.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I quit! I quit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.30,0:02:04.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How am I supposed to do this investigation?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.89,0:02:09.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything\Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.55,0:02:14.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here at the Central Command Center, \Nthere are brave soldiers who have no trouble
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.10,0:02:15.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,sacrificing whatever it takes in order to achieve peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.35,0:02:22.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are the tales of love and courage of the Flame Alchemist—Colonel Roy Mustang—and his men.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.92,0:04:02.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.21,0:04:04.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Black Hayate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.55,0:04:07.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure must be nice for you,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.88,0:04:09.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,leading a happy-go-lucky life.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.76,0:04:18.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with\NLieutenant Havoc?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.64,0:04:20.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He must've had his heart broken again or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.02,0:04:20.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was sharp.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.94,0:04:23.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't get much time off\Nwhen you take on military duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.69,0:04:26.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It must be hard finding a woman who will go out with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.11,0:04:28.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's pathetic.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.36,0:04:31.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he were a man, he'd find a way to handle both his work and women.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.20,0:04:32.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.99,0:04:37.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, as things are, \Nit's interfering with his duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.29,0:04:40.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, someone introduce a woman to Havoc.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.79,0:04:42.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please don't ask the impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.46,0:04:43.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want someone to introduce me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.83,0:04:45.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colonel, why don't you share one of yours?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.25,0:04:47.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.38,0:04:48.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.47,0:04:52.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does anyone know what\Nkind of woman Havoc likes?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.30,0:04:54.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, the other day, when I was out drinking with Havoc,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.93,0:04:59.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he complained to me, "Aren't there any \Ncheerful, well-adjusted beauties out there?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.35,0:05:00.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right, Warrant Officer Falman,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.81,0:05:03.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,secure a cheerful,\Nwell-adjusted beauty at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.48,0:05:04.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Introduce her to Lt. Havoc.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.65,0:05:05.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want {\i1}me{\i0} to?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.36,0:05:08.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Remember, you're on a mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.32,0:05:10.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a mission for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.07,0:05:13.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All the materials on Brig. Gen.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.61,0:05:15.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Basque Grand,\NDoctor Marcoh, and Shou Tucker.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.33,0:05:20.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Also, put together all the records on \Nthe 5th Laboratory and the 2nd Prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.62,0:05:21.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.62,0:05:24.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does that include the items\Nlost in the Central Library fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.92,0:05:26.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not ask me the obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.79,0:05:28.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is why I called on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.00,0:05:32.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If this can get me into the\NCourt-Martial Office again,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.97,0:05:35.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I might be able to more closely investigate the incident involving Brig. Gen. Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.68,0:05:36.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is your answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.68,0:05:38.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes! Understood!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.06,0:05:43.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A mission, he says.\NI haven't had any training in flirting.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.19,0:05:44.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the world coming to?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.03,0:05:51.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon!\NAre you all right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.65,0:05:52.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.57,0:05:53.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Warrant Officer Falman!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.82,0:05:57.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Long time no see.\NHave you been\Ngetting along okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.70,0:06:00.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...\Nmore or less.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.29,0:06:03.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.71,0:06:07.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka, I'm looking for a cheerful, well-adjusted beauty right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.50,0:06:08.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know anyone like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.84,0:06:11.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do I know anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.84,0:06:15.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So what you're insinuating is that I'm {\i1}not{\i0} a cheerful, well-adjusted beauty, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.13,0:06:16.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, it's not like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.26,0:06:18.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Under the Colonel's orders, I have to introduce Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.43,0:06:21.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc to a new girlfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.52,0:06:22.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Girlfriend?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.27,0:06:24.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have anyone in mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.64,0:06:26.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, in that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.35,0:06:27.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have a grand idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.65,0:06:31.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong's sister?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.94,0:06:32.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.99,0:06:36.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said that she is of marrying age but is so shy that she cannot find a boyfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.25,0:06:51.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.00,0:06:53.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think I'd better go...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.38,0:06:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.18,0:07:00.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If she starts talking about tying the knot, you'll be taking one wealthy wife!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.97,0:07:02.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll be on easy street!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.68,0:07:05.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I haven't even met her yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.19,0:07:10.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From what Major Armstrong says, \Nshe has the same dashing looks that he does.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.69,0:07:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Major's sister\Nlooks just like him?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.11,0:07:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it, I'm leaving!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.82,0:07:18.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you for coming, Lt.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.95,0:07:21.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.37,0:07:23.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been waiting for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.12,0:07:24.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, good luck!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.62,0:07:32.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Over the span of 180 years, the Armstrong family has been involved in enterprises
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.92,0:07:37.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that are deeply tied in with the political and economic affairs of this land.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.51,0:07:45.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For generations, it has been a noble family that has served in the military government
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.09,0:07:45.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and has been a pillar of support\Nto this nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.10,0:07:47.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I myself have served in\Nthe military government...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.73,0:07:51.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every time I hear Father tell the story, it is marvelous.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.02,0:07:52.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh my, Dear,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.15,0:07:55.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,are you boasting\Nto the guests again?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.73,0:07:56.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.28,0:07:58.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.53,0:08:00.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.16,0:08:03.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The mother is quite norm—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.74,0:08:05.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She's huge!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.08,0:08:07.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's not at all normal!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.58,0:08:11.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hold on a minute now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.08,0:08:14.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The father is wide and fat,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.88,0:08:16.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and the mother is long and tall.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.67,0:08:21.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Add them together, and their son\Nwould sum up like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.01,0:08:24.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means, when it\Ncomes to their daughter...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.56,0:08:34.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catch me if you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.48,0:08:38.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, both parents' features don't always necessarily get passed down.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.94,0:08:41.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a chance that she leans more toward one side.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.45,0:08:43.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, Lieutenant,\Nallow me to introduce my sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.45,0:08:45.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come along, Catherine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.83,0:08:47.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be shy. Come in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.71,0:08:50.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which is she?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.91,0:08:53.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does she take after her father, \Nor her mother?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.21,0:08:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I couldn't stand it either way, but between the two of them,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.21,0:08:56.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at least let her\Ntake after her mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.63,0:08:57.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.26,0:08:59.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.80,0:09:02.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.26,0:09:05.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm Catherine Elle Armstrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.60,0:09:07.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hooray for mutations!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.35,0:09:10.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well? Isn't she beautiful?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.89,0:09:11.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She looks just like me.\NWhich part?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.39,0:09:14.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her lower eyelashes, and such.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.61,0:09:15.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.02,0:09:17.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come now, Catherine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.44,0:09:18.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be shy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.86,0:09:19.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,R-Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.03,0:09:22.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, Catherine-san,\Nwhat are your hobbies?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.74,0:09:25.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see... a little piano...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.78,0:09:27.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.74,0:09:30.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way\Nthis girl is the Major's sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.00,0:09:35.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lift a little piano...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.42,0:09:37.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the matter, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.92,0:09:41.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I take that back.\NShe absolutely is the Major's sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.47,0:09:44.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But then again, if you take away her monstrous strength, there's...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.05,0:09:45.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her looks...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.05,0:09:46.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her figure...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.05,0:09:47.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her assets...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.01,0:09:48.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and her influence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.31,0:09:51.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does that make it all okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.23,0:09:52.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.60,0:09:54.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the prime of my life?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.44,0:09:57.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catherine-san...\NYes?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.27,0:09:58.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it's all right with you,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.02,0:10:01.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would you allow me\Nthe chance to go out with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.99,0:10:08.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Havoc-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.79,0:10:10.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.87,0:10:13.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.33,0:10:15.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.75,0:10:17.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.13,0:10:20.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,prefer men who are\Nmore like my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.47,0:10:28.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc-san, you are not my type, \Nso let's pretend we never spoke of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.51,0:10:30.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.60,0:10:32.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? What's the matter, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.56,0:10:34.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,10,000 cens says he blows it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.31,0:10:35.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,10,000 cens says she turns him down.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.94,0:10:38.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, 30,000 cens says\Nthey call the whole thing off.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.77,0:10:40.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That doesn't make for\Nmuch of a wager, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.57,0:10:41.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.40,0:10:45.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Why did I even come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.79,0:11:00.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, Major Armstrong is exactly the kind of man I figured him for.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.50,0:11:03.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Hawkeye, \Ncan you put out a dragnet?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.50,0:11:03.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.01,0:11:07.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.51,0:11:11.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had to go without lunch ever since I lost that bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.18,0:11:14.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won, so I've been\Neating my fill.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.35,0:11:16.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please buy me something!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.10,0:11:19.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I did that, the bet wouldn't mean anything, would it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.44,0:11:23.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aren't those fixed yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.19,0:11:26.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure do hate this.\NThe whole area is creepy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.99,0:11:29.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are even stories of ghosts appearing here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.71,0:11:39.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that sound?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.21,0:11:41.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.72,0:11:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.47,0:11:54.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.39,0:11:57.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.19,0:12:00.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're tickling me...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.99,0:12:13.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.83,0:12:17.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.25,0:12:19.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.50,0:12:20.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shake!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.58,0:12:21.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The other one!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.75,0:12:22.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lie down!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.92,0:12:23.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.39,0:12:39.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Lieutenant.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.56,0:12:39.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.77,0:12:41.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.02,0:12:42.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.94,0:12:44.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The stories are true!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.98,0:12:47.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give me a break! I won't be able to go out walking at night anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.07,0:12:49.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.74,0:12:51.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say they saw the 13th warehouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.82,0:12:52.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.24,0:12:55.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not nonsense, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.16,0:12:57.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right!\NWe really are scared here!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.41,0:12:59.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The 13th warehouse?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.33,0:13:03.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Military warehouses are only supposed to go up to the 12th warehouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.33,0:13:06.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say that there's \Na 13th one that appears!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.63,0:13:10.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In fact, they say that the location where it stands was an execution ground a long time ago!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.01,0:13:13.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When night falls,\Nthe 13th warehouse
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.55,0:13:16.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,appears in the place where\Nthere should only be twelve of them!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.43,0:13:19.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the ghosts of those who were executed there long ago
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.43,0:13:21.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can be heard scra... scraping,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.73,0:13:25.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,digging up the ground,\Nlooking for their own bodies!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.23,0:13:26.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ha! That's ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.73,0:13:31.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You look at things in a state of fear,\Nso you're just imagining the things\Nthat you're afraid of.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.44,0:13:32.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must've just mistook it\Nfor something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.16,0:13:34.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, aren't you afraid?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.87,0:13:35.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.99,0:13:37.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists are scientists.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.91,0:13:41.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's our job to always look at things\Nwith a logical mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.37,0:13:43.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we're not the\Nonly ones who saw it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.96,0:13:45.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are stories all over the Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.96,0:13:48.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is pathetic.\NYou call yourselves soldiers?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.67,0:13:51.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to reveal the reality of the situation
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.17,0:13:52.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to those who would spread these kinds of stories!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.09,0:13:54.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.68,0:13:55.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone, rejoice!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.80,0:13:58.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel says\Nhe's going to join our operation tonight!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.10,0:14:00.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's our colonel!\NHe thinks about his men!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.43,0:14:03.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! With the Colonel along, there's nothing to be afraid of!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.77,0:14:05.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute!\NWhat are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.52,0:14:08.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know, tonight's operation to uncover the truth about the ghostly phenomena.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.65,0:14:10.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to show us\Nthe reality of it, right, Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.11,0:14:12.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I did say that, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.86,0:14:15.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid to go home to the dorms at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.49,0:14:18.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please help us, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.04,0:14:26.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud, why do I have to \Ntag along on their little test of courage?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.96,0:14:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They all adore you, Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.09,0:14:31.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why should I be pleased\Nover being adored by men?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.30,0:14:34.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can men serve as soldiers against flesh-and-blood men,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.34,0:14:36.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when something they can't even see makes them jump out of their skin?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.19,0:14:47.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't tell you to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.27,0:14:49.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You looked like\Nyou wanted to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.78,0:15:00.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Colonel Mustang!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.87,0:15:03.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry to drop in on you\Nso unexpectedly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.29,0:15:05.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was just in the neighborhood.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.46,0:15:08.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, thank you for taking the trouble to see me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.21,0:15:10.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, Elicia,\Ncan you say hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.17,0:15:13.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey there, Elicia.\NHow are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.76,0:15:18.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, come on inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.97,0:15:20.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll serve some tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.10,0:15:29.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I still have\Nsome work to attend to,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.69,0:15:30.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so I'll be leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.86,0:15:34.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like I said...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.78,0:15:39.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's much more frightening to take on a live person.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.95,0:15:43.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Indeed, this is perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.24,0:15:44.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing in here about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.00,0:15:47.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't any more documents that Hughes left behind, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.16,0:15:48.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.71,0:15:50.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.33,0:15:52.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dispose of all of these materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.09,0:15:52.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't even leave ashes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.25,0:15:56.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But these are official \Nmilitary documents...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.13,0:15:56.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.47,0:16:02.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The 5th Laboratory\Nhad been shut down.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.26,0:16:04.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's only natural that there wouldn't be any records, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.89,0:16:06.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there are {\i1}too{\i0} few of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.93,0:16:10.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if it was shut down,\Nit's not natural for there not to be any records of installation maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.90,0:16:12.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone was\Nneglecting their duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.36,0:16:14.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean Brig. Gen. Grand?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.23,0:16:16.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you trying to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.99,0:16:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That it wasn't a mishap with the records, but that there {\i1}are{\i0} no records.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.49,0:16:23.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is evidence that there was\Na military directive to cover it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.20,0:16:28.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Though I couldn't imagine that the Führer was aware of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.29,0:16:31.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Chimeras that were\Nformed from humans...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.58,0:16:34.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Amplification of alchemic powers\Nby means of a Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.92,0:16:37.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Both would be powerful military assets in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.13,0:16:40.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You {\i1}do{\i0} know that those techniques are forbidden, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.13,0:16:43.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Science is the result\Nof trial and error.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.64,0:16:45.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Failing to utilize the mistakes of the past by learning from them,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.22,0:16:49.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and abandoning them as being too dangerous would be foolish, would it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.31,0:16:53.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, I have Zolf Kimbly and Shou Tucker under me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.15,0:16:55.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I would need is your order.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.77,0:16:59.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a rebellion\Nstarting up again in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.44,0:17:02.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is also intelligence that Scar is in hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.70,0:17:04.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How would you like to\Ntest your powers there?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.08,0:17:06.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.62,0:17:11.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For Pete's sake... For grown men to all gang up over some ghostly disturbance...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.54,0:17:13.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we really are frightened.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.38,0:17:15.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, having you along will be a great help.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.17,0:17:17.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's just investigate this quick\Nand go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.59,0:17:21.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From here on, the streetlights are out, so there's no light.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.88,0:17:24.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is Maintenance up to?! This is dereliction of duty!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.60,0:17:28.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That should do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.44,0:17:35.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just your shadow, you idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.06,0:17:38.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Fuery, if you do this, you can make shadows fun!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.44,0:17:41.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See? It's a cute doggie.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.74,0:17:42.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Woof! Woof!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.24,0:17:49.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop being so scared by everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.79,0:17:50.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's easy for you to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.75,0:17:51.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We really are scared!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.04,0:17:53.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.12,0:17:54.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You call yourselves my men?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.42,0:17:57.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on! I'll prove to you that there are no ghosts!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.63,0:17:59.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't leave us behind, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.80,0:18:02.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here is Warehouse 12.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.68,0:18:06.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Beyond it is just an empty lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.10,0:18:09.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look! Where do you\Nsee Warehouse 13?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.85,0:18:11.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's hiding because\Nthere are a lot of people here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.02,0:18:12.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Enough already!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.35,0:18:16.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could it be that they mean {\i1}that{\i0} \Nwhen they say 13?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.82,0:18:20.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The letter "B" from the alphabet.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.03,0:18:23.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looked like the number 13.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.61,0:18:25.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's true, you could mistake it for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.82,0:18:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, in the dark and out of fear, what you did was misread it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.45,0:18:30.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, you're such a scaremonger.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.95,0:18:33.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look! Once you realize what you're dealing with, that's all there is to it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.25,0:18:34.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what about the ghosts?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.66,0:18:36.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They don't exist!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.21,0:18:37.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.08,0:18:40.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now I can relax walking past here tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.25,0:18:42.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that you know,\Nwe're done here.\NLet's go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.51,0:18:45.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that I can relax,\NI'm feeling hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.47,0:18:46.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once we get back,\Nhow about some supper?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.01,0:18:48.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys are buying tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.39,0:18:50.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? I don't have any money!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.14,0:18:52.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what you get \Nfor scaring us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.56,0:18:52.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.89,0:18:53.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.85,0:18:54.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.56,0:18:57.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.48,0:18:59.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like something\Nwas dug up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.11,0:18:59.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.06,0:19:01.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Falman!\NRight.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.33,0:19:14.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.75,0:19:18.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A bone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.80,0:19:23.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure enough, it's the ghost of an executed prisoner!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.63,0:19:25.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It's really here!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.80,0:19:26.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Calm down!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.01,0:19:30.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if this were an execution grounds,\Nthey wouldn't be burying them here too, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.51,0:19:32.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a case of someone\Ndumping a body.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.56,0:19:36.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A body illegally dumped in a place \Nsaid to be a former execution grounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.64,0:19:40.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't any criminals who would come\Nall the way onto a military base just to bury this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.69,0:19:43.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means, you're saying that\Nthis is an incident internal to the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.03,0:19:45.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's highly possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.57,0:19:48.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's also possible that this bone belongs to a soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.17,0:20:05.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Establishing the identity of\Nthe victim is our top priority!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.42,0:20:06.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not overlook anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.05,0:20:08.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They won't necessarily be buried in just one spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.80,0:20:10.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dig up anywhere\Nthat looks suspicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.64,0:20:11.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.08,0:20:39.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, would you mind if I\Ntold you what I'm thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.09,0:20:47.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's the one who put us up to this nonsense?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.89,0:20:56.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.35,0:20:57.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.94,0:21:08.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.03,0:21:12.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, the tiger is on the move.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.41,0:21:16.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm looking forward to\Nhearing good things from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.45,0:21:17.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.83,0:21:19.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.58,0:21:22.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I request permission to go along with the dispatch eastward.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.67,0:21:26.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have requested Major Armstrong to oversee combat on this trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.54,0:21:30.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Major is staying\Noff the front lines\Ndue to the injuries he sustained in the recent fighting in Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.76,0:21:35.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I question whether the Major, who has not particularly distinguished himself in battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.93,0:21:35.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,should be given command of the forces on the front line.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.51,0:21:42.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I also have a responsibility to this case, \Nhaving once been stationed
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.97,0:21:42.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,at the Eastern Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.60,0:21:44.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please allow me to\Ngo along with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.19,0:21:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have no objections.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.52,0:21:49.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.94,0:21:51.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel Roy Mustang,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.57,0:21:54.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hereby order you to go along with\Nthe eastern suppression detachment.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.70,0:21:56.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I humbly accept your order!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.22,0:23:40.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.93,0:23:43.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 38: "With the River's Flow"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.02,0:23:48.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whenever I fought...\NWhenever I fought with Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.02,0:23:51.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would always hunch down on the bank of the river.
